From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 18:23:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: cubie-a7s: Supply the eMMC from
 the PMIC

The eMMC names two fixed regulators as supplies, but its rails are
SWOUT2 (3.3 V) and CLDO5 (1.8 V) of the AXP318W. Describe CLDO5 at its
single 1.8 V setting and use both rails; the fixed 1.8 V regulator goes.
CLDO5 keeps the name vcc-1v8, as vcc-pc would make the pin controller
take it as the bank PC supply, which is a change of its own.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; on the board with eMMC,
mmc2 takes vmmc from vcc-io and vqmmc from CLDO5, whose voltage register
in the PMIC reads back 1.8 V, comes up in HS400 enhanced strobe mode and
reads 256 MiB without errors. The other board has no eMMC.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts   | 21 +++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index 0e5b82aec3dd..b2cfae1c0449 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -58,15 +58,6 @@ scp@48100000 {
 		};
 	};
 
-	/* CLDO5 of the PMIC: VCC-PC and with it the eMMC VCCQ */
-	reg_vcc1v8: vcc1v8 {
-		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
-		regulator-name = "vcc-1v8";
-		regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
-		regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
-		regulator-always-on;
-	};
-
 	reg_vcc3v3: vcc3v3 {
 		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
 		regulator-name = "vcc-3v3";
@@ -114,8 +105,8 @@ &mmc0 {
 };
 
 &mmc2 {
-	vmmc-supply = <&reg_vcc3v3>;
-	vqmmc-supply = <&reg_vcc1v8>;
+	vmmc-supply = <&reg_swout2>;
+	vqmmc-supply = <&reg_cldo5>;
 	bus-width = <8>;
 	non-removable;
 	cap-mmc-hw-reset;
@@ -152,6 +143,14 @@ reg_dcdc1: dcdc1 {
 				regulator-always-on;
 			};
 
+			/* 1.8 V I/O: eMMC VCCQ, bank PC */
+			reg_cldo5: cldo5 {
+				regulator-name = "vcc-1v8";
+				regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
+				regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
+				regulator-always-on;
+			};
+
 			/*
 			 * Ethernet PHY, bank PD through R251, bank PJ, the
 			 * TWI2/TWI7 pull-ups on J11. Always on: bank PJ and the
